Description: Compares predicted protein-interaction neighbourhoods of
    transcript isoforms. The user supplies isoform seeds labelled "up" or
    "down", for example the isoforms that gain or lose usage in a
    differential transcript usage analysis. Each seed set is expanded in a
    bundled isoform-resolved predicted interaction network, or in a
    user-supplied igraph network, and the resulting neighbourhoods are
    compared per gene and summarised across genes. The package also provides
    connected-component analysis, network diagnostics, plots, and
    over-representation and gene set enrichment analysis of neighbourhood
    statistics. Protein-identical transcripts are resolved to shared
    representatives, and nonsense-mediated and non-stop decay transcripts,
    annotated from Ensembl through AnnotationHub, are excluded by default.
    Results are S4Vectors DataFrames, and gene sets can be GSEABase
    collections such as those of the msigdb package. Statistical testing of
    isoform usage remains upstream of the package.
